                            	   400: 
                            	   401: ; =============================================================================
                            	   402: ; OPEN ITEMS / not yet implemented:
                            	   403: ;
                            	   404: ; 1. sega_logo_tiles_8bpp — the actual converted tile pixel data. Needs an
                            	   405: ;    offline conversion tool (4bpp packed-nibble MD format -> 8bpp
                            	   406: ;    1-byte-per-pixel X68000 format). Not written yet; propose as the next
                            	   407: ;    concrete piece of work once this routine's structure is confirmed.
                            	   408: ;
                            	   409: ; 2. Joypad-driven early exit (Regis is redesigning this layer separately
                            	   410: ;    to support 2/3-button pads + keyboard; deliberately left out per
                            	   411: ;    conversation).
                            	   412: ;
                            	   413: ; 3. The one-shot pre-cycle fade-in nudge (see file header) — deferred,
                            	   414: ;    low visual impact, can revisit if needed after a side-by-side check.
                            	   415: ;
                            	   416: ; 4. DISABLE_INTERRUPTS/ENABLE_INTERRUPTS are no-ops in x68k_macros.i for
                            	   417: ;    Human68k user-mode reasons (see that file's comment). None of this
                            	   418: ;    routine's steps are timing-critical against interrupts the way the
                            	   419: ;    MD's DMA setup was, so no supervisor-mode workaround was needed here
                            	   420: ;    -- worth double-checking once we plug this into the real VBLANK-driven
                            	   421: ;    game loop rather than running it standalone at startup.
                            	   422: ; =============================================================================
                            	   423: 
                            	   424: ; =============================================================================
                            	   425: ; BSS
                            	   426: ; =============================================================================
